[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2408125273","pull_request_review_id":3306824880,"id":2408125273,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6PiRNZ","diff_hunk":"@@ -2001,7 +2001,9 @@ Vector<uint8_t> RenderingDevice::texture_get_data(RID p_texture, uint32_t p_laye\n \t\t\t// Assuming layers are tightly packed. If this is not true on some driver, we must modify the copy algorithm.\n \t\t\tDEV_ASSERT(mip_layouts[i].layer_pitch == mip_layouts[i].size / tex->layers);\n \n-\t\t\twork_buffer_size = STEPIFY(work_buffer_size, work_mip_alignment) + mip_layouts[i].size;\n+\t\t\t// Write current offset to the mip layout struct.\n+\t\t\tmip_layouts[i].offset = STEPIFY(work_buffer_size, work_mip_alignment);","path":"servers/rendering/rendering_device.cpp","commit_id":"82e8ae735902b6e8cbf8ebb46f79520f26bfb995","original_commit_id":"82e8ae735902b6e8cbf8ebb46f79520f26bfb995","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This overrides the offset set inside `texture_get_copyable_layout()` Can you explain why? Presumably that offset was correct for Vulkan and Metal before.\r\n\r\nIs it just that textures in Vulkan always used a tight layout so the offset doesn't matter there? \r\n\r\nI am not familiar with `GetCopyableFootprints()` but it is strange that it returns an offset that we can't use","created_at":"2025-10-06T19:26:52Z","updated_at":"2025-10-06T19:28:58Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111328#discussion_r2408125273","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111328","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2408125273"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111328#discussion_r2408125273"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111328"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2408125273/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":2005,"original_line":2005,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":6,"position":6,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2408350115","pull_request_review_id":3307097075,"id":2408350115,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6PjIGj","diff_hunk":"@@ -2001,7 +2001,9 @@ Vector<uint8_t> RenderingDevice::texture_get_data(RID p_texture, uint32_t p_laye\n \t\t\t// Assuming layers are tightly packed. If this is not true on some driver, we must modify the copy algorithm.\n \t\t\tDEV_ASSERT(mip_layouts[i].layer_pitch == mip_layouts[i].size / tex->layers);\n \n-\t\t\twork_buffer_size = STEPIFY(work_buffer_size, work_mip_alignment) + mip_layouts[i].size;\n+\t\t\t// Write current offset to the mip layout struct.\n+\t\t\tmip_layouts[i].offset = STEPIFY(work_buffer_size, work_mip_alignment);","path":"servers/rendering/rendering_device.cpp","commit_id":"82e8ae735902b6e8cbf8ebb46f79520f26bfb995","original_commit_id":"82e8ae735902b6e8cbf8ebb46f79520f26bfb995","user":{"login":"blueskythlikesclouds","id":19259897,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjU5ODk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19259897?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds","html_url":"https://github.com/blueskythlikesclouds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"D3D12 doesn't compute the offset value correctly at all at the moment. I was planning on making an issue about this inconsistency later, but if you prefer I could try to solve it in this PR.\r\n\r\nThe behavior is currently like this:\r\n\r\nVulkan: If TILING_LINEAR, Vulkan function is used to calculate the offset, which accounts for the layer. Otherwise, the layer is completely ignored.\r\nMetal: Ignores the layer.\r\nD3D12: Offset simply isn't computed correctly at all, it's always 0.\r\n\r\nThe copy function I changed was still broken technically. It assumed the mips were always going to be placed after each other tightly, even if there were different offset values in the mip layout.\r\n\r\nIt would be easy to make D3D12 account for either scenario, I'm just not sure what the intended behavior is supposed to be here with the `texture_get_copyable_layout()` function.","created_at":"2025-10-06T20:17:30Z","updated_at":"2025-10-06T20:25:11Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111328#discussion_r2408350115","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111328","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2408350115"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111328#discussion_r2408350115"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111328"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2408350115/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":2005,"original_line":2005,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2408125273,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":6,"position":6,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2409493813","pull_request_review_id":3308542697,"id":2409493813,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6PnfU1","diff_hunk":"@@ -2001,7 +2001,9 @@ Vector<uint8_t> RenderingDevice::texture_get_data(RID p_texture, uint32_t p_laye\n \t\t\t// Assuming layers are tightly packed. If this is not true on some driver, we must modify the copy algorithm.\n \t\t\tDEV_ASSERT(mip_layouts[i].layer_pitch == mip_layouts[i].size / tex->layers);\n \n-\t\t\twork_buffer_size = STEPIFY(work_buffer_size, work_mip_alignment) + mip_layouts[i].size;\n+\t\t\t// Write current offset to the mip layout struct.\n+\t\t\tmip_layouts[i].offset = STEPIFY(work_buffer_size, work_mip_alignment);","path":"servers/rendering/rendering_device.cpp","commit_id":"82e8ae735902b6e8cbf8ebb46f79520f26bfb995","original_commit_id":"82e8ae735902b6e8cbf8ebb46f79520f26bfb995","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"